From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:08:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm: add HDMI connector properties for side by side (full)
 timing and 3D metadata

Two things about a 3D mode belong to the sink, not to the mode, so they
are connector properties:

- "side by side full timing": "whole line doubled" (the default) times
  side by side (full) as HDMI 1.4a, Appendix H, Figure H-4 does, the
  whole line and the pixel clock doubled; "blanking kept" keeps the 2D
  horizontal blanking, as NVIDIA's driver does, for sinks that refuse the
  first. The picture and the buffer are the same in both. Drivers time
  stereo modes with drm_connector_stereo_crtc_flags() or, without a
  connector state at hand, drm_atomic_crtc_stereo_flags().

- "HDMI 3D metadata": a blob of struct drm_hdmi_3d_metadata, sent as the
  3D metadata of the HDMI vendor InfoFrame (Appendix H, Tables H-1 and
  H-4) while a 3D mode is set. Its one defined type is the parallax
  information of ISO/IEC 23002-3, which a sink needs to turn the depth of
  an L + depth picture into parallax; the compositor that draws the depth
  knows it. drm_hdmi_vendor_infoframe_set_3d_metadata() adds it to a
  vendor InfoFrame, and the HDMI state helper does so for its drivers.

The state helper also forces a modeset when the timing changes.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
